<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the App target.

  Mandatory since May 2024 for any bundle that calls a "required reason" API. The only one this
  target calls is UserDefaults, in SharedInboxPlugin.swift:20, reading what the Share Extension
  stashed in the App Group. Reason CA92.1 is the exact match: "Access info from same app, or app
  group your app is a member of."

  Deliberately NOT declared, because they are not required-reason APIs:
    - FileManager contents/removeItem/createDirectory (SharedInboxPlugin.swift:22, :31). The
      file-timestamp category (C617.1 etc.) covers creationDate / modificationDate /
      attributesOfItem only, none of which this app calls.
    - Location. CoreLocation is not a required-reason API; it is governed by the Info.plist usage
      string and the runtime prompt.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is intentionally omitted. It is required of third-party SDKs, not of
  apps, and the authoritative privacy label for an app is the App Privacy questionnaire in App
  Store Connect. Declaring it in both places invites a mismatch between them. THE QUESTIONNAIRE
  STILL HAS TO BE FILLED IN — this file does not replace it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
